  "estimatedMinutes": 2,
  "statement": "The solution of the equation \\(7^{x+7}=8^x\\) can be expressed in the form \\(x=\\log_b 7^7.\\) What is \\(b?\\)",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{15}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{7}{8}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{8}{7}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{8}\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(\\dfrac{15}{7}\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "c",
    "value": "8/7"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-12a-2010-p11.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Since \\(x=\\log_b 7^7,\\) we have \\(b^x=7^7.\\)\n\nThen \\[ \\begin{aligned} (7b)^x=7^x\\cdot b^x &= 7^x\\cdot7^7 \\\\ &= 7^{x+7}=8^x. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nBecause \\(x\\gt0,\\) it follows that \\(7b=8,\\) so \\(b=\\dfrac{8}{7}.\\)\n\nThus, C is the correct answer.",
      "hints": [
        "\\(x=\\log_b 7^7\\) means \\(b^x=7^7\\)",
        "Multiply to combine the bases: \\((7b)^x=7^x\\cdot b^x=7^{x+7}\\)"
      ],
      "images": []
    }
  ],
